I am thinking...: Now I need to understand the vulnerability. Looking at `ihevcd_ref_list`:

The arrays `ai4_poc_st_curr_before`, `ai4_poc_st_curr_after`, `ai4_poc_st_foll`, `ai4_poc_lt_curr`, `ai4_poc_lt_foll` are all `MAX_DPB_SIZE = 16` elements.

In the `ihevcd_ref_list` function, the loops iterate based on `num_neg_pics` and `num_pos_pics`:

```c
for(i = 0; i < num_neg_pics; i++)
{
    if(pi1_used[i])
    {
        ai4_poc_st_curr_before[u4_num_st_curr_before] = ...;
        u4_num_st_curr_before++;
    }
    else
    {
        ai4_poc_st_foll[u4_num_st_foll] = ...;
        u4_num_st_foll++;
    }
}
```

Now, `u4_num_st_curr_before` and `u4_num_st_foll` can go up to `num_neg_pics` combined.

Similarly for `num_pos_pics`:
```c
for(i = num_neg_pics; i < num_neg_pics + num_pos_pics; i++)
{
    if(pi1_used[i])
    {
        ai4_poc_st_curr_after[u4_num_st_curr_after] = ...;
        u4_num_st_curr_after++;
    }
    else
    {
        ai4_poc_st_foll[u4_num_st_foll] = ...;
        u4_num_st_foll++;
    }
}
```

And for long-term:
```c
for(i = 0; i < ps_slice_hdr->i1_num_long_term_sps + ps_slice_hdr->i1_num_long_term_pics; i++)
{
    ...
    if(ps_slice_hdr->ai1_used_by_curr_pic_lt_flag[i])
    {
        ai4_poc_lt_curr[u4_num_lt_curr] = i4_poc_lt;
        ai1_curr_delta_poc_msb_present_flag[u4_num_lt_curr] = ...;
        u4_num_lt_curr++;
    }
    else
    {
        ai4_poc_lt_foll[u4_num_lt_foll] = i4_poc_lt;
        ai1_foll_delta_poc_msb_present_flag[u4_num_lt_foll] = ...;
        u4_num_lt_foll++;
    }
}
```

The validation in `ihevcd_parse_slice_header.c` at line 474 checks:
```c
if((value + ps_slice_hdr->i1_num_long_term_sps + num_neg_pics + num_pos_pics) > (MAX_DPB_SIZE - 1))
```

This limits the total (num_long_term_pics + num_long_term_sps + num_neg_pics + num_pos_pics) to `MAX_DPB_SIZE - 1 = 15`.

But the arrays in `ihevcd_ref_list` can still overflow because `u4_num_st_curr_before` could reach up to `num_neg_pics` and `u4_num_st_foll` could get up from `num_neg_pics + num_pos_pics`, and so on. Wait, no - they add up to `num_neg_pics + num_pos_pics + num_long_term` total, which is limited to 15. So MAX_DPB_SIZE=16 should be enough.

Hmm, but wait. Let me look more carefully. The check in the parse_slice_header is:
```c
if((value + ps_slice_hdr->i1_num_long_term_sps + num_neg_pics + num_pos_pics) > (MAX_DPB_SIZE - 1))
```

This is only done when `ps_sps->i1_long_term_ref_pics_present_flag` is true! If long-term ref pics are not present, `num_neg_pics + num_pos_pics` are not bounded by this check.

What bounds `num_neg_pics` and `num_pos_pics`? Let me check the short-term ref pic set parsing.

Let me also look at what happens with the `as_ref_pic_list_temp0[MAX_DPB_SIZE]` array. The loop:
```c
u4_num_rps_curr_temp_list0 = (WORD32)u4_num_total_curr > ps_slice_hdr->i1_num_ref_idx_l0_active ? (WORD32)u4_num_total_curr : ps_slice_hdr->i1_num_ref_idx_l0_active;

r_idx = 0;
while(r_idx < u4_num_rps_curr_temp_list0)
{
    for(i = 0; (i < (WORD32)u4_num_st_curr_before) && (r_idx < u4_num_rps_curr_temp_list0); r_idx++, i++)
    {
        as_ref_pic_list_temp0[r_idx] = as_ref_pic_st_curr_before[i];
    }
    ...
}
```

If `u4_num_rps_curr_temp_list0` > MAX_DPB_SIZE, then `as_ref_pic_list_temp0[r_idx]` will overflow.

`u4_num_rps_curr_temp_list0 = max(u4_num_total_curr, ps_slice_hdr->i1_num_ref_idx_l0_active)`

And `ps_slice_hdr->i1_num_ref_idx_l0_active` can be up to `MAX_DPB_SIZE - 1 = 15` (validated at parse time), or it's set from `ps_pps->i1_num_ref_idx_l0_default_active`.

Wait, `i1_num_ref_idx_l0_active = value + 1`, and the check is `value > MAX_DPB_SIZE - 2` returns error. So `value <= MAX_DPB_SIZE - 2 = 14`, so `i1_num_ref_idx_l0_active <= 15`.

But `u4_num_total_curr` could potentially be larger if the short-term ref pic set allows more entries than MAX_DPB_SIZE. Let me check the short-term ref pic set parsing.

Actually, wait. Let me re-read the check. When `i1_long_term_ref_pics_present_flag` is false, there's no bound check on `num_neg_pics + num_pos_pics`. Let me find where `ihevcd_short_term_ref_pic_set` is defined.

